# `arguments` of sloppy functions: a parameter and its element are one variable, so a store to either shows in the other, until the element is deleted or redefined.
# With more and fewer arguments than parameters, `arguments.callee`, the length overwritten, the object leaked to a closure, returned and handed on.
# LIBRARY: own
# RUN: run-in-shell globalThis.report = value => print(String(value));
# CHECK: 10,2,2
# CHECK-NEXT: 10,undefined,1
# CHECK-NEXT: undefined,undefined,0
# CHECK-NEXT: 20,30
# CHECK-NEXT: 20,undefined
# CHECK-NEXT: undefined,undefined
# CHECK-NEXT: 5,5
# CHECK-NEXT: 6,6
# CHECK-NEXT: 8,8
# CHECK-NEXT: 2,2
# CHECK-NEXT: 1,undefined,undefined,8,7
# CHECK-NEXT: 2,8,undefined,8,7
# CHECK-NEXT: 3,8,7,8,7
# CHECK-NEXT: 1,undefined,9
# CHECK-NEXT: 3,9,9
# CHECK-NEXT: 4,2,2,1
# CHECK-NEXT: 1,2,undefined,1
# CHECK-NEXT: undefined,3,1
# CHECK-NEXT: 1,4
# CHECK-NEXT: 1,2,1
# CHECK-NEXT: undefined
# CHECK-NEXT: true
# CHECK-NEXT: 1
# CHECK-NEXT: 11
# CHECK-NEXT: 12
# CHECK-NEXT: 3,1,3,true
# CHECK-NEXT: 13
# CHECK-NEXT: 14,1
# CHECK-NEXT: 16,15
# CHECK-NEXT: 17,1
# CHECK-NEXT: 0|1|2;0|1|2|length|callee
# CHECK-NEXT: ;length|callee
# CHECK-NEXT: [object Arguments],object,false
# CHECK-NEXT: 18|2|3;18|2|3
# CHECK-NEXT: undefined,undefined,undefined,undefined,undefined
# CHECK-NEXT: 2,2,true,false
# CHECK-NEXT: undefined|1|2|undefined|
# CHECK-NEXT: undefined|1|2|3|4|undefined|
# CHECK-NEXT: undefined|undefined|
# CHECK-NEXT: 1|19|3|
# CHECK-NEXT: 1|
# CHECK-NEXT: 2
# CHECK-NEXT: 23
# CHECK-NEXT: true
# CHECK-NEXT: true
# CHECK-NEXT: 10,2,2;20,undefined;undefined|0|undefined|
# CHECK-NEXT: 10,2,2;20,undefined;undefined|1|undefined|
# CHECK-NEXT: 10,2,2;20,undefined;undefined|2|undefined|
# CHECK-NEXT: end
# CHECK-NEXT: exited with 0
